<title>THAILAND: Thailand to expand export credit to 20 bln baht.</title>
<headline>Thailand to expand export credit to 20 bln baht.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand, in a move to boost sagging exports, said on Wednesday it will raise the level of credit extended to exporters to 20 billion baht ($800 million) from this year against 1.6 billion baht previously.</p>
<p>Finance Minister Amnuay Viravan said his ministry would also reorganise its widely-criticised customs department to reduce red tape for exporters within one month. Exporters recently complained at a meeting with the government that the customs department was corrupt and its services were poor.</p>
</text>
